<BaseLayout title="Waterbear 40 Automatic Dive Watch | Will Chai" description="A watchmaking project by William Chai." path="/waterbear/"><div class="pageShell"><SiteHeader current="projects" /><main id="main" class="pageMain"><article class="archiveRecord"><p>Project archive</p><h1>Waterbear 40 Automatic Dive Watch</h1><p>Waterbear is a mechanical watch designed and assembled by William Chai under the WillChai name. The project takes its name from the tardigrade, commonly called a waterbear.</p><img src="/photography/shuffle/photo_243.avif" width="800" height="800" alt="WillChai Waterbear automatic watch" /><h2>The watch</h2><p>The original design pairs a 40 mm stainless steel case with a blue ceramic bezel, a textured blue dial, a sapphire crystal and a blue rubber strap. A Seiko NH35A automatic movement powers the watch.</p><p>The design was presented as an edition of 25 pieces. This page preserves the project record. For current availability and service enquiries, <a href="mailto:me@willchai.com">contact Will</a>.</p><p><a href="/projects/">Explore current projects</a></p></article></main><SiteFooter /></div></BaseLayout>
